      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1306319868,
      "text": "Aloe aculeata is an Aloe species that is native to the Limpopo valley and Mpumalanga in South Africa along with southern and central Zimbabwe and Mozambique. It grows on rocky outcrops in grassland and dry bushveld. Aculeata (\"prickly\") refers to the spines on the leaf's surface and the teeth on its margins."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Aloe aculeata",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloe_aculeata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 174847642,
      "text": "Aloe aculeata es una especie del género Aloe, originaria de Sudáfrica."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Aloe aculeata",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloe_aculeata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 232888989,
      "text": "Aloe aculeata est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Xanthorrhoeaceae. C'est un aloès natif des régions de Limpopo et de Mpumalanga en Afrique du Sud, mais également situées le long du centre et du sud du Mozambique et du Zimbabwe."
    },
